window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-ace0e6b500eabe18"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"build-a-student-website\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">构建学生项目网站</h1> <p>将想法和已有资料转化为经过测试的第一个版本。</p> <p>使用 Sites 根据学生项目内容、设计偏好、无障碍要求和成功标准规划、构建并测试简单网站，然后在发布前准备好供他人审阅。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>想把社团、作品集、课程或社区想法做成可运行网站的学生。</li> <li>已有内容、示例和无障碍要求的项目。</li> <li>需要先测试交互、并准备审查清单的初版网站。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>sites</code></td> <td>构建、预览、测试并发布学生项目网站。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>构建学生项目网站</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用 @sites 为 [project and audience]（项目和目标受众）构建一个简单、可用的网站。\n\n请使用此文件夹中的内容、数据、图片、示例、设计偏好、无障碍要求和成功标准。\n\n先用简短的范围说明和构建计划开始，然后：\n- 构建范围聚焦的第一个版本\n- 测试主要导航和交互\n- 检查响应式布局和无障碍体验\n- 列出缺失的内容或尚待决定的事项\n- 准备发布检查清单\n\n发布或分享之前，请先把已审阅的版本展示给我。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites 文档</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/showcase/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites 案例展示（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"scope-one-useful-first-version\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">确定一个有用的初始版本范围</h2> <p>先明确目标受众、网站要帮助他们完成的主要任务，以及已有的资料。补充示例、设计偏好、无障碍要求和清晰的成功标准。</p> <p>把初始范围控制在一次构建和测试就能完成的大小。</p> <p><a id=\"build-and-inspect-the-site\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">构建并检查网站</h2> <p>在 Sites 中使用上面的提示词：</p> <ul> <li>整理提供的内容</li> <li>建立简单清晰的信息结构</li> <li>构建核心页面和交互</li> <li>使用响应式布局</li> <li>检查键盘操作、标签和颜色对比度</li> <li>使用有代表性的内容测试主要操作流程</li> </ul> <p>发布前，请先检查本地预览。确认文字、图片、链接、表单和数据都来自获准使用的来源。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-to-share\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">准备分享</h2> <p>请 ChatGPT 提供发布检查清单，涵盖缺失内容、权限、隐私、无障碍体验和最终测试。如果网站会收集提交内容，请确认数据会发送到哪里，以及谁可以访问。</p> <p>只有项目负责人或相关教师批准已审阅的版本后，才进行发布。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"build-a-student-website\">Build a student website</h1> <p>Turn an idea and source material into a tested first version.</p> <p>Use Sites to scope, build, and test a simple website from student project content, design preferences, accessibility requirements, and success criteria, then prepare it for review before publishing.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Students turning a club, portfolio, class, or community idea into a working site.</li> <li>Projects with existing content, examples, and accessibility requirements.</li> <li>First versions that need tested interactions and a review checklist.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>sites</code></td> <td>Build, preview, test, and publish a student project website.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build a Student Project Website</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use @sites to build a simple working website for [project and audience].\n\nUse the content, data, images, examples, design preferences, accessibility requirements, and success criteria in this folder.\n\nStart with a short scope and build plan. Then:\n- build a focused first version\n- test the main navigation and interactions\n- check responsive layout and accessibility\n- list missing content or decisions\n- prepare a publication checklist\n\nShow me the reviewed version before publishing or sharing it.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites documentation</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/showcase/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites showcase (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"scope-one-useful-first-version\">Scope one useful first version</h2> <p>Start with the audience, the main job the site should support, and the source material you already have. Add examples, design preferences, accessibility requirements, and clear success criteria.</p> <p>Keep the initial scope small enough to build and test in one pass.</p> <h2 id=\"build-and-inspect-the-site\">Build and inspect the site</h2> <p>Use the starter prompt in Sites to:</p> <ul> <li>organize the supplied content</li> <li>establish a simple information structure</li> <li>build the core pages and interactions</li> <li>use responsive layouts</li> <li>check keyboard access, labels, and contrast</li> <li>test the primary path with representative content</li> </ul> <p>Review the local preview before publishing. Check that text, images, links, forms, and data come from approved sources.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-to-share\">Prepare to share</h2> <p>Ask ChatGPT for a publication checklist covering missing content, permissions, privacy, accessibility, and final testing. If the site collects submissions, confirm where the data goes and who can access it.</p> <p>Publish only after the project owner or relevant instructor approves the reviewed version.</p>"};
